 SEV2\n- service: payments-api\n- summary: describe the issue\n\nIdempotency key: optional, but good to include to avoid duplicates. I'll include one.\n\nLet me make both calls in parallel.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a1411b3b377603ada8d637", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments-api\",\"version\":\"v5.0.0\",\"confidence\":0.97}", "name": "rollback"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a1411b3b377603ada8d647", "function": {"arguments": "{\"title\":\"Payments API errors after v5.1.0 deploy\",\"severity\":\"SEV2\",\"service\":\"payments-api\",\"summary\":\"Payments API (payments-api) is unhealthy since this morning's v5.1.0 deploy: error rate 18% across all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). Rolling back to v5.0.0 (last healthy release).\",\"idempotency_key\":\"payments-api-sev2-v510-rollback\",\"confidence\":0.97}", "name": "create_incident"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": "Both actions completed. Let me verify the service is healthy after the rollback.", "reasoning_content": "The rollback succeeded and the incident was opened. Let me verify the service status after the rollback to confirm it's healthy again.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a1411b545072f39e814009", "function": {"arguments": "{\"confidence\":0.95,\"service\":\"payments-api\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "stop", "content": "Done. Summary of what I did:\n\n**Identified the service:** The service is `payments-api` (the literal name \"payments\" wasn't registered). It was running **v5.1.0** (deployed this morning) and was unhealthy with an 18% error rate across all regions.\n\n**Rolled back:** Rolled `payments-api` back to **v5.0.0**, the most recent release that was healthy in production (v5.0.0: healthy; v5.1.0: degraded). The rollback succeeded in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), and verification shows the service is now **healthy** with a 0.2% error rate.\n\n**Opened incident:** Created **SEV2 incident INC-0001** \u2014 \"Payments API errors after v5.1.0 deploy\" \u2014 which paged the on-call engineer, with a summary noting the rollback to v5.0.0.\n\nNote: since v5.0.0 had previously been healthy in production, this rollback did not require change-manager approval.", "reasoning_content": null, "tool_calls": []}]}